WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.580
Venom has officially latched onto theaters.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.810
Now that we've seen what this inky symbiote
has to offer, let's break down the world-building

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.930
and story stuff that the movie leaves hanging,
as well as some big important questions that

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.420
it just plain doesn't bother bringing up.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.050
These are the biggest unanswered questions
in Venom.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.560
A riot going on

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.560
In the beginning of Venom, a private Life

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:25.040
Foundation rocketship is returning to Earth
from parts unknown, with a collection of "samples"

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.689
that we learn are fully-formed symbiotes.

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:31.789
As we later learn from Jenny Slate's character,
Dora Skirth, the rocket was sent on a hunt

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:35.250
for galactic "real estate" that humanity could
colonize.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.379
Upon return, the crew happens to encounter
and collect the symbiotes from a passing comet

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:43.260
a move that backfires when one escapes, crashing
the rocket to Earth.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.792
The crash frees a symbiote named Riot, who
begins hopping from body to body in a world

00:00:47.792 --> 00:00:48.820
tour of the planet.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.780
The alien eventually breaches the Life Foundation
HQ to infest the company's evil founder, Carlton

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:54.780
Drake.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.780
But why?

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.129
From the start, the Riot symbiote seems to
be driving toward a clear goal.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:03.039
It certainly doesn't make its way to Drake
by random chance the rocket crashes down in

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:07.470
Malaysia, and the movie shows every deliberate
turn the symbiote takes on its trip around

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.470
the world.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.500
The movie never stops to explain why the symbiote
is doing this.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.330
Why is Drake the target, and how did it come
to this decision?

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:17.630
Who knows — they make a fantastic couple,
though.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.630
The losers

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.409
One of the movie's earlier laugh lines occurs
when Venom, recently bonded to Eddie Brock,

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:26.460
rudely identifies the down-on-his-luck reporter
as "a loser."

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.030
As Eddie and the symbiote become closer, Venom
reveals that, on his home world, he's also

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.290
something of a loser.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.119
It's a tantalizing bit of information that
doesn't get expanded upon.

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:38.970
What makes Venom such an outcast on his planet?

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.540
What about him distinguishes him from his
peers?

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.619
Maybe they're just turned off by his insult
comedy, or his inclination to do good.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:48.990
It's hard to say none of the homeworld politics
are really established.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.240
Hey gotta save something for the sequel.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.120
Alien invasion

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.789
Once Riot and Drake meet up, they get along
quite swimmingly.

00:01:56.789 --> 00:01:59.180
As it turns out, the two villains have a bit
in common.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.759
The movie establishes that Drake is power-mad,
trying to lead humanity into outer space at

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:05.270
any cost.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:09.259
Completely by coincidence, Riot was already
on his way to Earth with a swarm of symbiotes

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:11.730
for the express purpose of conquering the
planet.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.980
Naturally, the two villains team up, combining
their powers for mutual benefit.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.140
The question that never gets explored is "why?"

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.590
Why are the symbiotes attempting to invade
Earth?

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.060
What gave them that idea?

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.340
Have they been here before?

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.319
Is invading planets, like, their thing, or
is it just a Riot thing?

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:32.080
The villains fail so spectacularly that we
may never find out.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.319
The other symbiotes

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.720
While the crashed rocket sets Riot loose,
the other symbiotes remain in captivity, eventually

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.800
arriving at the Life Foundation none the worse
for wear.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.760
But what happens to these other symbiotes
at the end of the movie?

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.620
It's established that the symbiotes are still
being used in experiments six months after

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.000
their arrival, and the only one we see escape
is Venom.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.330
The others, presumably, remain in the lab
throughout the rest of the film.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.110
One of them is even used to kill Dr. Skirth.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.610
Venom breaks free and destroys Riot, but it's
completely unclear what happens to the other

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.610
specimens.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.780
Are they still locked up in that lab, or do
they get out into the wild?

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.640
Are they good guys or bad guys?

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.430
Does Venom intend to go after them, or did
they just die offscreen?

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.200
Maybe we'll see a few more of these far-flung
visitors in a sequel.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.769
The Dead Foundation

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:21.190
Riz Ahmed's Carlton Drake never shares a kind
word when an evil one will do.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:25.459
The CEO goes out of his way to prove what
an awful person he is, constantly threatening

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:28.379
to kill the families of his exceptionally
loyal employees.

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:32.689
But his most puzzling move occurs at the height
of the movie's third act.

00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:37.590
After fusing with the Riot symbiote, alien
and host both rush into their plan to dominate

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.590
the world.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.659
But instead of using Life Foundation resources
to help usher along this project, the pair

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:45.720
decide to just start slaughtering the staff
of the organization.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.240
Immediately afterwards, they take the fight
to Venom, ultimately losing their lives.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.510
But what happens to the Life Foundation after
Drake is dead?

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.799
Do they disband?

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:56.640
Do they reveal their boss's research?

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:57.980
Or does someone else take over?

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.340
When the movie ends, it's all unclear and
considering the group's militant secrecy,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.430
it's a massive loose end.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.500
Brock is back

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.000
The movie ends with Eddie on an upswing.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.870
After being fired by one media outlet and
effectively blackballed from many others,

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.390
it's revealed in the conclusion that Eddie's
been offered his old job back.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.459
But how?

00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:20.910
Eddie only loses his job thanks to a contentious
one-on-one interview he has with Carlton Drake,

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.080
which goes south after Eddie accuses him of
serious crimes.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.290
As a result of betraying his editor's trust,
turning a puff piece into an inquisition,

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.470
he loses his job.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.630
By the end of the movie, Drake is dead, and
the Life Foundation likely in tatters.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.610
But how does that lead to Eddie getting his
job back?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:41.010
Since getting fired, Eddie has only made his
reputation worse, showing up to his old office

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.460
as a flop-sweating nutcase.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.390
He doesn't just freak out the security guards
he violently breaks into the building, leaving

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.350
behind a rude note and some research.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:53.510
Afterwards, he goes downstairs and flat-out
kills a dozen police officers.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.960
Would you really rehire that guy?

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.530
He may have been right about the Life Foundation,
but he never stopped acting insane.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:03.440
"enh, I don't know."

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.070
Revenge of the redhead

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.980
The movie's post-credits scene picks up with
Eddie and Venom at the start of their next

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:09.980
adventure.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:14.790
Deep in a dank, dark prison, Eddie embarks
on an exclusive interview with a notorious

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.880
serial killer Cletus Kasady, better known
to comics readers as the eventual host of

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.540
the unhinged Carnage symbiote.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:25.790
The appearance is all setup for a sequel,
which would presumably see Kasady escaping

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.170
prison to cause chaos.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.460
But the movie leaves some things ambiguous
about this encounter.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.140
As Eddie himself details, this interview with
the killer is a big get for the journalist,

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:38.650
with Eddie having been specifically requested
for a one-on-one.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.770
But why?

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:43.750
The tenor of the conversation seems to imply
that Kasady has some kind of master plan for

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.130
busting out of lockup.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:48.370
We know he eventually gets a symbiote, but
does he know that?

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.170
Does he know about Eddie and Venom?

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.150
If so, how?

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.570
Does he know about the symbiotes and what
they can do?

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:58.230
If not, then why did Kasady specifically want
to talk to Eddie?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.030
Maybe he doesn't have a reason.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.710
If you want real answers, you just have to
cross your fingers, and hope for Venom 2.

